{
  "_description": "The evidence for the 480 thumns of the Warsh muṣḥaf: the divisions the printed muṣḥaf marks only in its margin. The build adds them to the ۞ the docx prints inline and to the opening of the Qurʾān at 1:1, and gets 435 + 44 + 1 = 480; it fails if that total does not close (pipeline/qurantext/divisions.py). The result is published as `hizb_starts` and `thumn_starts` in data/mushaf/warsh.json. Nothing here is a word number: each entry is keyed by this edition's own `ayah`, and its division starts at that āyah's first word. `page` is this edition's.",
  "_checked": "Every label in the print was located, not only the ones listed here: each page was rendered, each label in the outer margin was found by its position, and its page and row were matched to the data. All 479 labels fell on a ۞ or on an entry below, and no label was left over. Then the label at every ḥizb start, and every label listed here, was read.",
  "_labels": "`label` is the margin text as printed, without its vowel marks. This print words its labels: «حزب» at a ḥizb start, «الجزء N الحزب M» where a juz starts too, then «ثمن», «ربع», «ثمن», «نصف الحزب», «ثمن», «ربع», «ثمن». The third quarter reads «ربع», not «ثلاثة أرباع».",
